# Mirror CI's "i18n catalog + manifest" gate so a missing key or a stale
# manifest.json never reaches a push (and a red CI run). Both checks are
# sub-second and need no build. See grimoire/CLAUDE.md for the i18n workflow.
pnpm i18n:check
node scripts/gen-locale-manifest.mjs --check

# Mojibake guard. v1.26.1 shipped 77 cp1252-round-tripped sequences because the
# corruption is invisible in review and the fix happened to sit uncommitted in
# the working tree. This is the cheapest place to catch a recurrence.
pnpm encoding:check

# Second half of the upstream backlink guard (commit-msg is the first). Amends,
# rebases and cherry-picks can all rewrite a message past that hook, and the
# push is the moment GitHub gets to act on it. Upstream's own "(#326)" squash
# subjects are exempt: they are already reachable from upstream/main.
pnpm refs:check

# This is where the repo keeps its cheap invariant gates. Protects a workflow
# file (.github/workflows/release.yml) that only changes locally before it is
# pushed: catching a loosened engine pin here is earlier than catching it in
# an actual release run.
pnpm engine-pin:check
